From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 17:50:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] nexell: add arm64 (S5P6818) SoC support

Mainline mach-nexell only ever built the 32-bit S5P4418; the S5P6818
Kconfig symbol selected ARM64 but nothing consumed it and several pieces
did not compile/link for arm64:

  * boot0.h emitted the 32-bit ARM_VECTORS + embedded-NSIH layout, which
    is meaningless on arm64. The S5P6818 boot.img wrapper prepends the
    NSIH+BL1 externally, so on ARM64 the raw binary only needs a reset
    branch at its entry point.
  * nx_i2c.c selected the S5P4418/S5P6818 stop-condition path with a
    runtime IS_ENABLED(), so the inactive branch (referencing members
    that only exist for the other SoC) still had to compile and failed.
    Use preprocessor guards instead.
  * ARCH_S5P6818 did not select OF_CONTROL/NX_GPIO/DM_SERIAL/PL01X_SERIAL
    the way ARCH_S5P4418 does.
  * No arm64 SoC glue existed (arch_cpu_init, reset_cpu, print_cpuinfo,
    enable_caches, the MMU mem_map). Add cpu-s5p6818.c, the armv8
    counterpart of arch/arm/cpu/armv7/s5p4418/cpu.c, and build the
    nexell PWM timer only on S5P4418 (arm64 uses the generic timer).

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 arch/arm/dts/Makefile                     |   3 +-
 arch/arm/mach-nexell/Kconfig              |  14 ++-
 arch/arm/mach-nexell/Makefile             |   3 +-
 arch/arm/mach-nexell/cpu-s5p6818.c        | 116 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm/mach-nexell/include/mach/boot0.h |   9 ++
 drivers/i2c/nx_i2c.c                      |  48 +++++----
 6 files changed, 169 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/mach-nexell/cpu-s5p6818.c

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/Makefile b/arch/arm/dts/Makefile
index 2b65cd91..6573d5a5 100644
